    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.files\n\n### Question\n\nWhen using `mini.starter` and then open `mini.files` with `MiniFiles.open(vim.api.nvim_buf_get_name(0))` the path will be not valid since it will be opening `<project-path>/Starter`. I've been trying to check the path first but still no luck. I'm also jump around using telescope search files from kickstart.nvim and when using `MiniFiles.get_latest_path()` it still opening the 'root' working directory. Is there a way to fix it when open `mini.files` while on `mini.starter` buffer? ",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.files</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">When using <code class=\"notranslate\">mini.starter</code> and then open <code class=\"notranslate\">mini.files</code> with <code class=\"notranslate\">MiniFiles.open(vim.api.nvim_buf_get_name(0))</code> the path will be not valid since it will be opening <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;project-path&gt;/Starter</code>. I've been trying to check the path first but still no luck. I'm also jump around using telescope search files from kickstart.nvim and when using <code class=\"notranslate\">MiniFiles.get_latest_path()</code> it still opening the 'root' working directory. Is there a way to fix it when open <code class=\"notranslate\">mini.files</code> while on <code class=\"notranslate\">mini.starter</code> buffer?</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.files\nQuestion\nWhen using mini.starter and then open mini.files with MiniFiles.open(vim.api.nvim_buf_get_name(0)) the path will be not valid since it will be opening <project-path>/Starter. I've been trying to check the path first but still no luck. I'm also jump around using telescope search files from kickstart.nvim and when using MiniFiles.get_latest_path() it still opening the 'root' working directory. Is there a way to fix it when open mini.files while on mini.starter buffer?",
